		{"time": "1:36", "joke": "playing yume nikki - "The Weeknd Looking Around" GIF."},
		 References how Yume Nikki's gameplay is mainly based on wandering around various worlds, which are often labyrinthine and easy to get lost in, and finding interesting things over more traditional gameplay objectives.   
		{"time": "1:39", "joke": "Hiveswap fans betting on which terrible business decision What Pumpkin will make next - A scene from the Jack Ryan episode "Black 22" where Victor Polizzi pushes his chips in."},
		 References Hiveswap's troubled development, as well as What Pumpkin, the company responsible for publishing and managing Hiveswap and the larger Homestuck franchise.   
		{"time": "1:42", "joke": "I think Matpat will enjoy dissecting this frame by frame - A clip of "The Brick Wall "Talks Politics"" by Marionzo Vance."},
		 References a series of tweets from tinyBuild, the publisher of the Hello Neighbor franchise, which attempted (and failed) to convince MatPat to analyze Hello Neighbor: The Animated Series as part of his Game Theory series.   
		{"time": "1:44", "joke": "Omori fans when ayo the pizza here - An edited clip of the Breaking Bad episode "Hermanos" where Gus Fring stands silently in an elevator."},
		 Refers to the "Ayo the pizza here" Vine by CalebCity, which in turn is often associated with a major plot point of OMORI.   
		{"time": "1:47", "joke": "The Escapist fans getting themselves arrested so they can play their favourite game in real life - A clip of Bobby Brown from The Bobby Brown Story getting arrested while smiling."},
		 References the setting of The Escapist, prison.   
		{"time": "1:50", "joke": "Night in the Woods fans 92% of the way into the chill slice of life coming of age story - A clip of the Zombie Land Saga episode "Good Morning SAGA" where Minamoto Sakura gets hit by a truck."},
		 References the sudden horror-esque events that happen very far into Night in the Woods' story.   
		{"time": "1:52", "joke": "Vampire Survivors fans when they go shopping on black friday - A clip from the video "Extreme Whipcracker: Adam Winrich" by Volume One"},
		 References the main gameplay loop of Vampire Survivors (slaughtering crowds of enemies with weapons).   
		{"time": "1:55", "joke": "Outer Wilds fans when you spoil that there's a spaceship in the game without a two paragraph content warning and a password authenticated spoiler tag - A clip of the "honey trial" scene from Bee Movie where Layton reacts hysterically after getting stung by Adam."},
		References how the Outer Wilds' community dislikes people revealing spoilers since it's a knowledge-based game meant to be played blind.   
		{"time": "1:58", "joke": "Disco Elysium fans in their basement writing Animal Farm fanfiction - The "Gunna Writing Fire" GIF."},
		 References how the differing political ideologies of people and nations play important roles in Disco Elysium's plot and setting, with the slander poking fun at how such a politically-charged game might seem to be an unusual match for a conventional fandom (Animal Farm being a political satire by George Orwell).   
		{"time": "2:00", "joke": "Slay the Spire fans crafting their perfect Blasphemy + Vault synergy - A clip of from the music video for "Get Your Shine On" by Birdman ft. Lil Wayne of Birdman rubbing his hands together while looking out a window."},
		 Using the Blasphemy + Vault synergy combo in Slay the Spire instantly kills the player.   
		{"time": "2:03", "joke": "Henry Stickmin fans when they don't get to retry from the last decision after dying a horrifying and painful death - A GIF of a sped up skeleton burning with flames surrounding it."},
		References the Replay mechanic in the Henry Stickmin franchise, in which players are allowed to reload save files to choose alternative story choices.   
		{"time": "2:06", "joke": "Lisa fans when they hear someone having an aneurysm on the keyboard - A clip from the Sesame Street song "Change the Plan"."},
		 References the unusual instrumentation and samples used in LISA: The Painful songs such as "All Hail the Fishmen" and "Work Harder".   
		{"time": "2:09", "joke": "Average yiik fan - A GIF of a custom "Chad Thundercock"-themed fighter striding from Soulcalibur VI."},
		 References the ironic popularity of YIIK: A Post-Modern RPG.   
		{"time": "2:11", "joke": "BitTripRunner fans 2023 meetup - A clip of The Fresh Prince of Bel Air episode "I, Done" where Will ponders over the Banks family's empty living room."},
		The slander pokes fun of the niche popularity of BIT.TRIP RUNNER, implying that the game isn't popular enough to warrant a sizeable fanbase.   
		{"time": "2:14", "joke": "Va-11 hall-a fans concocting the most revolting beverage imaginable - A scene from the Breaking Bad episode "Sunset", where Walter White is seen manufacturing drugs."},
		 Refers to the main gameplay mechanic of creating drinks based on clients' preferences to reveal story elements in VA-11 Hall-A: Cyberpunk Bartender Action. The caption itself references the "Weebs making the worst memes in existence" meme using the aforementioned Breaking Bad scene.   {"time": "2:17", "joke": "Your Turn To Die fans when Joe Mama - A clip from the SpongeBob SquarePants episode "Fools in April" where Squidward laughs hysterically when pranking SpongeBob."},
		 References the character Joe Tazuna from Your Turn to Die -Death Game By Majority- and how often he is used to reference the "Joe Mama" meme.   
		{"time": "2:19", "joke": "Bendy and the Ink Machine fans in the mall when they see a cardboard cutout - This GIF of a store employee grabbing an axe."},
		 References the usage of Bendy cardboard cutouts as setpieces/jumpscares in both Bendy and the Ink Machine and Bendy and the Dark Revival.   
		{"time": "2:22", "joke": "Slender fans in the same mall eyeing the mannequins in the menswear section - This GIF of a girl doing the "I'm watching you!" gesture."},
		References the faceless depiction of the Slenderman and how he looks like a mannequin.   
		{"time": "2:25", "joke": "Garten of Banban players after finishing the game realizing they've had the best video game experience of all time - A clip of Thanos smiling from Avengers: Infinity War."},
		References the mass ironic fandom of the Garten of Banban series.   
		{"time": "2:27", "joke": "FNF fans in 2054 still waiting for the game to come out - A clip from Saving Private Ryan where a young Ryan crossfades into his elderly self."},
		 References the extended development time of Friday Night Funkin' (the first release of the demo in 2020 to the current development of the full title as of 2023).   {"time": "2:30", "joke": "Geometry Dash fans rushing to flood the comment section on the latest obscure Newgrounds song used in the new hardest demon level - A GIF of a large crowd of people rushing into a store."},
		 Custom Geometry Dash levels uploaded by players allow the usage of audio uploaded to Newgrounds instead of/alongside official levels' song. As a result, when a level gets popular, players will often visit and comment on the audio said level used.   
		{"time": "2:32", "joke": "Eversion - A GIF sequence of the "Mr. Incredible Becoming Uncanny" meme."},
		 References the main mechanic of Eversion, which involves changing the current stage's state to a slightly different version of the stage, and this ability can be used recursively. Progressing through a level may require the player to go through multiple versions of the same level, each of which become more progressively gruesome and disturbing the deeper the player goes.   
		{"time": "2:35", "joke": "Iconoclasts fans when they see a pool of milk - This GIF of a woman jumping down the side of a cliff in heels."},
		 References ivory, a white liquid that is an essential source of power in the Iconoclasts universe.   
		{"time": "2:38", "joke": "Pizza Tower fans visiting the grave of historic war hero William S. Notty - This GIF of a person breakdancing while putting a shirt on."},
		 References Peppino's Breakdance mechanic in Pizza Tower and the mechanic of Snotty found within the tower.   
		{"time": "2:40", "joke": "Shmegdul Bobbin's Vacuuming Adventure fans when they finally beat Whirbert Hoover with no custom nozzles - A clip of Geometry Dash player npesta reacting to beating the custom level Kenos, originating from this YouTube video."},
		References the first slander joke in this rip (see 0:08 above).   {"time": "2:43", "joke": "Average Shovel Knight enjoyer - A GIF sequence of the "GigaChad" meme."},
		 "X Slander" videos usually end with a "GigaChad" GIF captioned with "Average X Enjoyer", with the X being the title of a media the video creator likes"}],
